"When ego blinds, one cannot have a calm live\nAs it's easy to do nothing, it's hard to forgive\n\nIt fuel wars and clouds empathy\nIt corrupts the mind like a plague\nAnd after the loss, attracts sympathy\nMakes the justifications, way too vague\n\nEven a slightest drop of this poison\nShall break bonds without a single thought\nThe aftermath makes the eyes moisen\nBut the actions were something the drinker ought\n\nIt's like a drug\nJust too addictive to quit\nFills the venomous mug\nMakes life's fuel, way too lit\n\nIt shatters families\nIt scatters the people\nIt creates anomalies\nBreaks the threads, by excess gripple\n\nYes it gives a boost for work\nAnd we cannot deny the efficiency\nBut it kills the choice to smirk\nWillingly, happily, calmly, without contingency\n\nIt ruins friendships\nIt destroys chosen bonds\nIt kills all relationships\nWhether platonic or not\n\nPlease control it, and burry \nDo not bring it between your favs\nIt'll ruin everything, with no sorry\nAnd then the regret? You'll endlessly crave"